=== HOOK_PORT ===
useDriving.ts left intact this prompt -- the hook already imports
'Drive as ApiDrive' from '../types' (api/types.ts) for getDrives. The
remaining hook return types (useDrive -> DriveDetail, useDriveTelemetry ->
DriveTelemetryPoint[], useDriveScore -> DriveScore, etc.) intentionally
continue using the legacy camelCase types from '@/types/driving' because:
  1. resilience.ts:camelCaseKeys aliases every snake_case JSON field to
     its camelCase equivalent at runtime, so callers get a superset of the
     legacy interface for free.
  2. Many of the legacy domain types (DrivingStats / DrivingDynamicsData /
     DrivetrainHealthData / RegenEfficiencyData / RouteEfficiencyData
     legacy shape / DrivingCoachData / TripPlan*) have no equivalent in
     api/types.ts -- these would have to be regenerated in a separate
     prompt 0011-style sweep before they can be ported.
  3. Phase-43 / Prompt 0021 (charging) used the same conservative pattern:
     the hook file itself was untouched and only field-formatting
     migrations happened in the consuming page (ChargingDetailPage).
URL audit on the hook: every request() call uses a path WITHOUT the
/api/v1/ prefix and snake_case query params (vehicle_id, days, q, ids).

=== PAGE_PORT ===
Modified files:
  web/src/features/driving/components/drive-detail/useDriveDetailData.ts

Migrations performed:
  1. Telemetry temperature fields (inside_temp / outside_temp / driver_temp /
     passenger_temp) switched from useSettings.convertTemp to
     convertTempFromSI(value, unitPrefs.temperature). Functionally
     equivalent for valid inputs but standardised on the new SI surface.
  2. Telemetry distance fields (ideal_range / rated_range / est_range /
     odometer) switched from useSettings.convertDistance (mph-input) to
     convertDistanceFromSI(meters, unitPrefs.distance). PRE-FIX BEHAVIOUR
     WAS BROKEN: telemetry values were already SI metres but were being
     passed to a converter that expects miles, so a 100,000 m odometer
     reading was being shown as either '100000 mi' or '160934 km'.
  3. Telemetry speed (m/s SI) switched from convertSpeed (mph-input) to
     convertSpeedFromSI(mps, unitPrefs.speed). Same root cause as #2.
  4. Tire-pressure fields (Pa SI) switched from convertPressure (bar-input)
     to convertPressureFromSI(pa/1000, unitPrefs.pressure). Same root
     cause -- bar converter on Pa input produced ~1000x wrong values.
  5. routeSource speed remains in raw m/s SI; speed-segment colour
     thresholds rewritten to SI (m/s) constants so colours are unit-agnostic.
  6. Drive aggregate fields kept on legacy useSettings.convertX:
     - drive.distanceMi -> convertDistance (genuine miles after SQL adapter)
     - drive.maxSpeedMph / avgSpeedMph -> convertSpeed (genuine mph)
     - drive.outsideTempAvgC / insideTempAvgC -- not consumed in this hook.

Other 11 driving pages + 30+ components UNCHANGED this prompt:
  All of them consume aggregate Drive fields (distanceMi/avgSpeedMph),
  DrivingStats (totalDistanceKm/avgSpeedKmh -- legacy backend wire-format),
  DrivingDynamicsData / DrivingCoachData / DrivetrainHealthData (own field
  shapes; backend reconciliation deferred). Same locked-policy continuation
  pattern as Phase-43/0021 charging (which migrated 1 of 10 pages and
  documented the rest as deferred).

